WEBVTT

1
00:00:00,568 --> 00:00:07,307
[♪♪♪]

2
00:00:16,684 --> 00:00:23,457
[♪♪♪]

3
00:00:31,966 --> 00:00:35,335
[WAVES CRASHING]

4
00:00:50,484 --> 00:00:57,391
[♪♪♪]

5
00:01:12,006 --> 00:01:14,074
SAM:
<i>60% of all professional killers</i>

6
00:01:14,141 --> 00:01:16,811
<i>grow a conscience</i>
<i>as mid-life approaches,</i>

7
00:01:16,878 --> 00:01:18,478
<i>but in my line of work,</i>

8
00:01:18,546 --> 00:01:21,983
<i>there's no such thing</i>
<i>as a retirement plan.</i>

9
00:01:22,050 --> 00:01:23,685
<i>Instead, you get me.</i>

10
00:01:26,453 --> 00:01:29,456
[GUNSHOTS]

11
00:01:29,524 --> 00:01:36,430
[♪♪♪]

12
00:01:44,005 --> 00:01:47,407
[♪♪♪]

13
00:01:53,982 --> 00:01:56,249
[CARTRIDGE AND HAMMER CLICKING]

14
00:02:04,826 --> 00:02:06,259
[DOOR CREAKS OPEN]

15
00:02:08,395 --> 00:02:13,233
Turn around.
Put your weapon down.

16
00:02:17,471 --> 00:02:20,575
I got a deal for you.
You walk away, you live.

17
00:02:24,612 --> 00:02:25,546
SAM:
<i>Hold up.</i>

18
00:02:25,613 --> 00:02:28,482
<i>Let's go back a bit,</i>
<i>see how we got here.</i>

19
00:02:35,288 --> 00:02:37,692
<i>My mark is an assassin</i>
<i>who disappeared on the job</i>

20
00:02:37,759 --> 00:02:39,927
<i>a few years ago.</i>

21
00:02:39,994 --> 00:02:41,596
<i>He's been a tough one to find.</i>

22
00:02:42,563 --> 00:02:46,199
<i>Turns out he's now</i>
<i>an art dealer for exclusive--</i>

23
00:02:46,266 --> 00:02:48,603
<i>Let's just say</i>
<i>not exactly legal pieces.</i>

24
00:02:49,604 --> 00:02:51,238
<i>Because of that,</i>
<i>he only takes meetings</i>

25
00:02:51,304 --> 00:02:53,508
<i>from referrals he trusts.</i>

26
00:02:54,642 --> 00:02:57,177
<i>And it just so happens</i>
<i>the dirt bag I'm gonna see</i>

27
00:02:57,244 --> 00:03:00,213
<i>now is a direct line to him.</i>

28
00:03:01,516 --> 00:03:03,250
<i>Now I don't usually</i>
<i>involve civilians</i>

29
00:03:03,316 --> 00:03:04,552
<i>or anyone outside my target,</i>

30
00:03:04,619 --> 00:03:08,556
<i>but this guy,</i>
<i>he's a grade A piece of shit.</i>

31
00:03:09,289 --> 00:03:14,062
<i>He sells women, drugs, guns,</i>

32
00:03:14,128 --> 00:03:15,763
<i>even kids</i>
<i>to the ultra-wealthy.</i>

33
00:03:17,230 --> 00:03:18,933
<i>I'm gonna be doin'</i>
<i>the world a favor.</i>

34
00:03:19,000 --> 00:03:25,773
[♪♪♪]

35
00:03:34,015 --> 00:03:40,788
[♪♪♪]

36
00:03:49,030 --> 00:03:55,803
[♪♪♪]

37
00:04:03,243 --> 00:04:04,612
-[MUFFLED GUNSHOT]
-[GROANS]

38
00:04:04,679 --> 00:04:11,586
[♪♪♪]

39
00:04:18,960 --> 00:04:19,994
[MUFFLED GUNSHOTS]

40
00:04:20,061 --> 00:04:26,768
[♪♪♪]

41
00:04:39,247 --> 00:04:40,681
[MESSAGES BEEPING]

42
00:04:47,255 --> 00:04:49,056
[CAR WHOOSHES]

43
00:04:49,123 --> 00:04:50,992
SAM:
<i>My job is to find and eliminate</i>

44
00:04:51,058 --> 00:04:52,860
<i>retired assets.</i>

45
00:04:52,927 --> 00:04:56,664
<i>I don't care how long it takes,</i>
<i>I will finish the job.</i>

46
00:04:57,965 --> 00:05:00,433
<i>I kill the best of the best.</i>

47
00:05:00,501 --> 00:05:04,572
<i>I'm an assassin of assassins,</i>
<i>a killer of killers.</i>

48
00:05:06,439 --> 00:05:08,209
<i>I didn't just fall</i>
<i>into this profession</i>

49
00:05:08,276 --> 00:05:10,443
<i>like so many others,</i>

50
00:05:10,511 --> 00:05:12,780
<i>I was an orphan of circumstance.</i>

51
00:05:13,915 --> 00:05:17,384
<i>I chose to hunt down the most</i>
<i>dangerous people on the planet,</i>

52
00:05:17,450 --> 00:05:20,588
<i>and make it my life's work,</i>

53
00:05:20,655 --> 00:05:23,624
<i>and I take great pride</i>
<i>in what I do.</i>

54
00:05:30,164 --> 00:05:31,464
[CAR DOOR OPENS]

55
00:05:37,104 --> 00:05:38,471
[CAR DOOR SHUTS]

56
00:05:39,339 --> 00:05:42,442
[BIRDS CHIRPING IN BACKGROUND]

57
00:05:43,110 --> 00:05:45,847
[GATE CLUNKS]

58
00:05:50,483 --> 00:05:52,352
Good morning,
I'm Mr. Anthony.

59
00:06:02,063 --> 00:06:03,463
Beautiful home.

60
00:06:03,531 --> 00:06:06,100
Yes, it is.
It's my retirement home.

61
00:06:06,167 --> 00:06:07,301
You're retired?

62
00:06:07,367 --> 00:06:10,504
I am. I am.
Um, but it didn't suit me well.

63
00:06:12,139 --> 00:06:13,774
I understand that.

64
00:06:15,509 --> 00:06:17,645
I don't think
I could ever retire.

65
00:06:20,014 --> 00:06:21,381
Well...

66
00:06:23,351 --> 00:06:24,685
Would you like to sit?

67
00:06:24,752 --> 00:06:25,786
Thank you.

68
00:06:25,853 --> 00:06:27,822
[GLASSES CLINKING]

69
00:06:36,530 --> 00:06:38,733
So tell me exactly
what you're looking for.

70
00:06:41,168 --> 00:06:43,070
A Rembrandt.

71
00:06:43,137 --> 00:06:44,305
A Rembrandt.

72
00:06:44,372 --> 00:06:46,040
I think I have two of those.

73
00:06:46,674 --> 00:06:48,441
I'm not looking
for just any Rembrandt.

74
00:06:48,509 --> 00:06:50,978
There's one in particular.

75
00:06:52,346 --> 00:06:53,814
You know which one?

76
00:06:55,216 --> 00:06:56,183
Sea of Galilee.

77
00:06:56,250 --> 00:06:58,686
[LAUGHS]

78
00:06:58,753 --> 00:07:00,554
You might as well be looking
for Christ.

79
00:07:00,621 --> 00:07:02,323
Everybody's looking
for that one.

80
00:07:02,390 --> 00:07:03,891
No one's found it.

81
00:07:05,226 --> 00:07:08,896
Yeah. But I think I just did.

82
00:07:13,534 --> 00:07:15,736
You're not who
I thought you were.

83
00:07:18,072 --> 00:07:20,942
No, I'm not.

84
00:07:24,245 --> 00:07:26,414
How'd you find me?

85
00:07:26,479 --> 00:07:28,382
It wasn't as hard as you think.

86
00:07:28,448 --> 00:07:30,584
But why, after five years,

87
00:07:30,651 --> 00:07:32,420
you come looking for me
after all this time?

88
00:07:32,485 --> 00:07:36,057
The way I see it,
we're both professionals.

89
00:07:36,123 --> 00:07:37,792
Or you were.

90
00:07:39,093 --> 00:07:40,561
Consider this a courtesy.

91
00:07:40,628 --> 00:07:42,930
If I was ever in your position,
I'd want the same thing.

92
00:07:46,634 --> 00:07:48,669
Don't you ever get tired
of this job?

93
00:07:48,736 --> 00:07:50,137
No.

94
00:07:50,204 --> 00:07:51,439
But I'm not you,

95
00:07:51,505 --> 00:07:54,375
and all those things
that you've done.

96
00:07:54,442 --> 00:07:55,910
That's why I'm here.

97
00:08:00,214 --> 00:08:01,816
Hmm.

98
00:08:04,251 --> 00:08:05,619
[HAMMER CLICKS]

99
00:08:08,456 --> 00:08:10,524
You younger breed,

100
00:08:10,591 --> 00:08:14,095
you know nothing,
you never have an exit strategy.

101
00:08:14,161 --> 00:08:15,796
Too many video games.

102
00:08:17,331 --> 00:08:20,301
And you older breed,

103
00:08:20,368 --> 00:08:24,138
you know nothing
about technology.

104
00:08:24,205 --> 00:08:26,107
[GUN MOUNT WHIRS]

105
00:08:26,173 --> 00:08:27,775
-[GUNSHOT]
-[EXPLOSION]

106
00:08:29,310 --> 00:08:32,246
[BULLET WHOOSHING]

107
00:08:32,313 --> 00:08:39,086
[♪♪♪]

108
00:08:47,328 --> 00:08:54,101
[♪♪♪]

109
00:09:02,343 --> 00:09:09,116
[♪♪♪]

110
00:09:17,358 --> 00:09:24,131
[♪♪♪]

111
00:09:32,373 --> 00:09:39,146
[♪♪♪]

112
00:09:47,388 --> 00:09:54,161
[♪♪♪]

113
00:10:02,403 --> 00:10:09,176
[♪♪♪]

114
00:10:17,418 --> 00:10:24,191
[♪♪♪]

115
00:10:32,433 --> 00:10:39,206
[♪♪♪]

116
00:10:47,448 --> 00:10:54,221
[♪♪♪]

117
00:11:02,463 --> 00:11:09,236
[♪♪♪]

118
00:11:17,478 --> 00:11:19,280
[GROANS]

119
00:11:19,346 --> 00:11:20,582
[ELEVATOR DINGS]

120
00:11:20,649 --> 00:11:23,484
[INDISTINCT CHATTER
IN BACKGROUND]

121
00:11:23,552 --> 00:11:30,691
[♪♪♪]

122
00:11:38,465 --> 00:11:40,467
[ELEVATOR DINGS]

123
00:11:40,535 --> 00:11:43,170
[INDISTINCT CHATTER
IN BACKGROUND]

124
00:11:46,641 --> 00:11:49,578
[HORSES GALLOPING]

125
00:11:49,644 --> 00:11:52,913
[INDISTINCT CHATTER]

126
00:12:00,522 --> 00:12:01,789
AUGUSTUS:
Yes.

127
00:12:01,855 --> 00:12:04,158
400 fuckin' thousand dollars
to win.

128
00:12:04,225 --> 00:12:07,294
If I wanted across the board,
I'd have fuckin' said it!

129
00:12:07,361 --> 00:12:08,796
All of it, to win!

130
00:12:08,862 --> 00:12:11,899
[CROWD CLAMORING IN BACKGROUND]

131
00:12:20,508 --> 00:12:22,810
You bet on Bing Bong Bing?

132
00:12:22,876 --> 00:12:25,513
Gambling isn't exactly
advisable in my line of work.

133
00:12:25,580 --> 00:12:26,981
Well, suit yourself.

134
00:12:27,047 --> 00:12:28,516
But I've got a feelin'
this long shot's

135
00:12:28,583 --> 00:12:30,217
gonna come through.

136
00:12:30,284 --> 00:12:32,019
I bet on a sure thing.

137
00:12:32,086 --> 00:12:34,121
I assume you received
your instructions okay.

138
00:12:34,188 --> 00:12:35,122
SAM:
I did.

139
00:12:35,189 --> 00:12:37,659
I'll take care
of the accommodations myself.

140
00:12:37,726 --> 00:12:39,026
I'll be in touch.

141
00:12:40,261 --> 00:12:45,199
Mr. Hayden, when I put
my money down on anything,

142
00:12:45,266 --> 00:12:47,234
it's never a gamble.

143
00:12:47,301 --> 00:12:49,236
I bet on a sure thing.

144
00:12:52,707 --> 00:12:54,808
SAM:
<i>Augustus is a smug prick,</i>

145
00:12:54,875 --> 00:12:57,144
<i>but he's also my boss.</i>

146
00:12:57,211 --> 00:13:00,014
<i>He runs what we call</i>
<i>the "organization".</i>

147
00:13:00,080 --> 00:13:01,849
<i>It's a loose net</i>
<i>of wealthy gangsters</i>

148
00:13:01,915 --> 00:13:05,919
<i>who control a vast network</i>
<i>of assassins for hire.</i>

149
00:13:05,986 --> 00:13:07,656
<i>I'm an assassin,</i>
<i>but I only kill wolves</i>

150
00:13:07,722 --> 00:13:09,223
<i>to protect the sheep.</i>

151
00:13:10,224 --> 00:13:12,694
<i>Every assignment</i>
<i>has its pros and cons.</i>

152
00:13:12,761 --> 00:13:14,895
<i>The pros of this one,</i>

153
00:13:14,962 --> 00:13:16,864
<i>the target's hiding out</i>
<i>right on my doorstep</i>

154
00:13:16,930 --> 00:13:19,867
<i>and I get to make</i>
<i>a long overdue trip home.</i>

155
00:13:19,933 --> 00:13:23,203
<i>The cons? This motherfucker.</i>

156
00:13:23,772 --> 00:13:26,206
<i>Charles Managold.</i>

157
00:13:27,174 --> 00:13:28,942
<i>Now, I don't get nervous</i>
<i>or intimidated</i>

158
00:13:29,009 --> 00:13:33,782
<i>by any target because,</i>
<i>well, I'm the best.</i>

159
00:13:33,847 --> 00:13:37,184
But if I did,
Managold would do it.

160
00:13:37,251 --> 00:13:38,152
[PLANE WHOOSHES]

161
00:13:38,218 --> 00:13:39,820
SAM: <i>A born killer</i>
<i>who won't let anything</i>

162
00:13:39,887 --> 00:13:42,156
<i>or anyone stand in his way.</i>

163
00:13:42,890 --> 00:13:46,226
<i>He doesn't care who or where.</i>

164
00:13:46,293 --> 00:13:49,296
<i>If he accepts the contract,</i>
<i>someone's gonna die.</i>

165
00:13:50,632 --> 00:13:52,433
<i>Now he's my contract.</i>

166
00:13:53,535 --> 00:13:54,835
<i>How the hell did this happen?</i>

167
00:13:54,902 --> 00:13:58,205
[DETECTOR BLIPPING]

168
00:13:58,272 --> 00:14:05,179
[♪♪♪]

169
00:14:07,381 --> 00:14:08,949
Fuckin' tracker.

170
00:14:09,617 --> 00:14:11,285
Really, Augustus?

171
00:14:12,453 --> 00:14:14,088
[TRACKER THUDDING]

172
00:14:14,154 --> 00:14:15,356
Prick.

173
00:14:18,859 --> 00:14:22,162
[CAR DOOR OPENS AND SHUTS]

174
00:14:28,369 --> 00:14:29,470
[CAR ENGINE WHIRS]

175
00:14:32,406 --> 00:14:34,542
SAM:
<i>Mine is a nomadic existence,</i>

176
00:14:34,609 --> 00:14:36,977
<i>and that suits me just fine,</i>

177
00:14:37,044 --> 00:14:39,279
<i>or else I'm in the wrong line</i>
<i>of work.</i>

178
00:14:39,346 --> 00:14:41,949
[CAR WHOOSHES]

179
00:14:42,015 --> 00:14:44,351
SAM: <i>In this business,</i>
<i>you don't have friends.</i>

180
00:14:45,687 --> 00:14:49,591
<i>You don't have relationships,</i>
<i>because they'll find out</i>

181
00:14:49,657 --> 00:14:51,258
<i>and that's what gets you killed.</i>

182
00:14:53,160 --> 00:14:56,063
<i>You can't have any weaknesses.</i>

183
00:14:56,130 --> 00:14:58,232
<i>Weaknesses are exploited.</i>

184
00:15:00,234 --> 00:15:04,004
<i>But everyone needs a place</i>
<i>to call home,</i>

185
00:15:04,071 --> 00:15:05,807
<i>somewhere completely</i>
<i>off the grid</i>

186
00:15:05,874 --> 00:15:07,809
<i>where they'll never find you.</i>

187
00:15:07,876 --> 00:15:09,176
[CAR DOOR SHUTS]

188
00:15:10,277 --> 00:15:11,579
[CAR DOOR OPENS]

189
00:15:11,646 --> 00:15:14,415
SAM: <i>Somewhere that feels like</i>
<i>a breath of fresh air.</i>

190
00:15:15,717 --> 00:15:16,885
[CAR DOOR SHUTS]

191
00:15:16,950 --> 00:15:19,953
[BIRDS CAWING AND CHIRPING
IN BACKGROUND]

192
00:15:20,755 --> 00:15:22,489
SAM:
<i>Somewhere to feel safe.</i>

193
00:15:22,557 --> 00:15:29,329
[♪♪♪]

194
00:15:35,068 --> 00:15:36,504
[BIRDS CHIRPING IN BACKGROUND]

195
00:15:36,571 --> 00:15:37,471
Finally.

196
00:15:37,539 --> 00:15:39,039
Hi.

197
00:15:39,874 --> 00:15:41,175
Welcome home.

198
00:15:41,241 --> 00:15:44,612
It's good to be home.
I missed you.

199
00:15:44,679 --> 00:15:46,213
Hmm.

200
00:15:47,381 --> 00:15:51,084
Mm, you get a shower
before you get any of this.

201
00:15:52,921 --> 00:15:54,689
You're gonna be
the death of me.

202
00:15:54,756 --> 00:15:56,256
If you're lucky.

203
00:15:56,323 --> 00:15:57,257
[DOOR OPENS]

204
00:15:57,725 --> 00:15:59,661
[THUMP]

205
00:15:59,727 --> 00:16:00,994
[CLUNK]

206
00:16:03,698 --> 00:16:04,566
[THUS]

207
00:16:05,800 --> 00:16:07,434
[CURTAIN SCRAPES]

208
00:16:07,502 --> 00:16:08,368
[TAP SQUEAKS]

209
00:16:08,435 --> 00:16:11,338
[WATER RUNNING]

210
00:16:20,849 --> 00:16:22,416
You see who it is?

211
00:16:23,083 --> 00:16:25,052
Yeah, just another cliché.

212
00:16:25,118 --> 00:16:27,020
An assassin
who grew a conscience.

213
00:16:27,087 --> 00:16:29,256
That's Charles Managold.

214
00:16:29,323 --> 00:16:30,592
Yeah.

215
00:16:30,658 --> 00:16:31,960
He's a legend.

216
00:16:32,025 --> 00:16:33,761
SAM:
They all are.

217
00:16:33,828 --> 00:16:35,062
NONA:
Chuparosa?

218
00:16:35,128 --> 00:16:37,364
SAM:
Everyone's heard of Chuparosa.

219
00:16:37,932 --> 00:16:40,067
Range, 1,900 yards.

220
00:16:40,133 --> 00:16:42,436
Velocity, 2,008 feet per second.

221
00:16:42,504 --> 00:16:44,238
[FRIDGE DOOR OPENS]

222
00:16:44,304 --> 00:16:46,541
Bullet drop, wind speed,
curvature of the earth...

223
00:16:46,608 --> 00:16:48,008
[ICE CUBES CLINK]

224
00:16:48,075 --> 00:16:49,911
...all factored in.

225
00:16:49,978 --> 00:16:50,812
[FRIDGE DOOR SHUTS]

226
00:16:50,879 --> 00:16:52,379
Bullets don't fly straight.

227
00:16:52,446 --> 00:16:54,414
It's a common misconception,
especially at that range.

228
00:16:55,282 --> 00:16:58,418
They come right down
on your head.

229
00:16:58,485 --> 00:17:00,722
And by doing so,
he killed an innocent woman

230
00:17:00,788 --> 00:17:02,022
in the process.

231
00:17:02,089 --> 00:17:05,125
Went through her
to hit his mark.

232
00:17:05,192 --> 00:17:07,027
Charles Managold
would've killed his own mother

233
00:17:07,094 --> 00:17:08,863
if that meant completin' a job.

234
00:17:08,930 --> 00:17:11,231
[BOTTLE CLUNKS]

235
00:17:11,298 --> 00:17:13,100
First off, goin' through
an innocent woman

236
00:17:13,166 --> 00:17:15,770
to hit his mark
is a hell of a shot.

237
00:17:15,837 --> 00:17:18,472
Second, things change.

238
00:17:19,373 --> 00:17:21,676
God knows what would make
a sick fuck like that

239
00:17:21,743 --> 00:17:23,076
not follow through.

240
00:17:23,845 --> 00:17:25,813
He's ruthless, Sam.

241
00:17:26,748 --> 00:17:29,416
I think you of all people know
how ruthless I can be, Nona.

242
00:17:32,486 --> 00:17:34,989
Besides, I think
if I didn't know any better,

243
00:17:35,055 --> 00:17:37,157
you're kinda worried about me.

244
00:17:39,393 --> 00:17:41,729
You should try bein' afraid
more often, you know?

245
00:17:41,796 --> 00:17:43,363
Nah.

246
00:17:47,200 --> 00:17:49,604
You never could refuse me, Sam.

247
00:17:49,671 --> 00:17:53,073
I'm the ring that's missin'
in your chain mail armor.

